{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"diagnosis\":\"The existing proof is valid but repeatedly unpacks bisimilarity witnesses and converts derivative relations back with `le_bisimilarity`. Calling `follow_fst` and `follow_snd` directly on homogeneous bisimilarity avoids that duplication and reduces both proof syntax and elaboration work.\",\"proof_body\":\"by\\n  intro h\\n  use @ChoiceBisim _ _ defs, ChoiceBisim.choice h\\n  intro s₁ s₂ hs μ\\n  cases hs with\\n  | bisim h =>\\n    constructor\\n    · intro s₁' ht\\n      obtain ⟨s₂', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n      exact ⟨s₂', ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n    · intro s₂' ht\\n      obtain ⟨s₁', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n      exact ⟨s₁', ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n  | choice h =>\\n    constructor\\n    · intro s₁' ht\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨s₂', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_fst ht\\n        exact ⟨s₂', Tr.choiceL ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        refine ⟨s₁', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim ?_⟩\\n        apply HomBisimilarity.refl\\n    · intro s₂' ht\\n      cases ht with\\n      | choiceL ht =>\\n        obtain ⟨s₁', ht', h'⟩ := h.follow_snd ht\\n        exact ⟨s₁', Tr.choiceL ht', ChoiceBisim.bisim h'⟩\\n      | choiceR ht =>\\n        refine ⟨s₂', Tr.choiceR ht, ChoiceBisim.bisim ?_⟩\\n        apply HomBisimilarity.refl\"}"}}
